menu "Input device board resources"

    config APP_IMU_CAPTURE
        bool "Bounded raw IMU diagnostic capture"
        default n
        help
            Observe accepted ordered board samples in a fixed PSRAM buffer.
            A Mouse Motion rising edge begins a capture; disabling Motion or
            filling 6000 records ends it. Records are formatted and dumped
            later through the existing diagnostic console, at most one per
            coordinator loop. The observer never changes motion policy or
            reads the sensor. Full storage stops capture, not mouse input.
            This is a diagnostic build option, not a new motion estimator.

    config APP_DISPLAY_SPI_QUEUE_DEPTH
        int "Mosaico display SPI transaction queue ceiling"
        range 1 2
        default 1
        help
            Limit queued transactions for the Mosaico CO5300 panel only.
            The pinned BSP uses PSRAM draw buffers with internal DMA bounce
            buffers. Each queued chunk retains up to 8190 payload bytes with
            the pinned S31 bus configuration, plus allocation metadata.
            A ceiling of one limits that payload to 8190 bytes; two permits
            16380 bytes. The SDK recycles chunks while sending the entire
            viewport and retains the existing TE and final completion path.
            Increasing this ceiling requires a complete internal/DMA memory
            budget and device throughput qualification.

endmenu
